      {
        "question_text": "Evaluate $12^{2}-9\\times\\sqrt{4}$.",
        "solution_text": "$12^{2}-9\\times\\sqrt{4}$\n$=144-9\\times 2$\n$=144-18$\n$=126$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A student writes:\n$\\left(\\sqrt{81}-\\sqrt{36}\\right)^{2}=\\left(\\sqrt{81}\\right)^{2}-\\left(\\sqrt{36}\\right)^{2}=81-36=45$\nExplain what is wrong and give the correct value.",
        "solution_text": "The index applies to the whole bracket, so the subtraction inside must be done first; a power cannot be shared out over a subtraction.\n$\\left(\\sqrt{81}-\\sqrt{36}\\right)^{2}$\n$=(9-6)^{2}$\n$=3^{2}$\n$=9$"
      }
